      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): mark connected status degraded without bot identity",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen Slack `auth.test` fails at boot, or `channels.slack.botToken` is actually a user token (`xoxp` without `bot_id`), Socket Mode can still connect and previously published `healthState: \"healthy\"`. Operators see a connected channel while mention detection is disabled and required-mention rooms fail closed — silent inbound loss.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTransport liveness (`connected: true`) is still useful, but advertising `healthy` is wrong when bot identity is missing. Publish `healthState: \"degraded\"` with `lastError` instead, and log `slack socket mode connected (degraded identity)`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Misconfigured bot tokens / failed `auth.test` no longer look healthy in channel status.\n- Valid bot-token installs are unchanged (`healthy` on connect).\n\n## Evidence\n\n### L1\n- Unit: `publishSlackConnectedStatus(..., { degraded: true })` asserts `healthState: \"degraded\"` and `lastError` in `provider.reconnect.test.ts`.\n\n### L3 live (redacted) — real Slack workspace `hah`\n\nUsed live Bot User OAuth Token (`xoxb-…REDACTED`) and User OAuth Token (`xoxp-…REDACTED`) via local env only (not committed). **Rotate these tokens if they were pasted into chat.**\n\n**BEFORE (old always-healthy on connect):**\n```json\n{\n  \"connected\": true,\n  \"healthState\": \"healthy\",\n  \"lastError\": null\n}\n```\n\n**LIVE `auth.test` with bot token:**\n```json\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"user_id\": \"U0BFV1X131V\",\n  \"bot_id\": \"B0BGACNKEGJ\",\n  \"team\": \"hah\"\n}\n```\n\n**LIVE `auth.test` with user token misused as botToken:**\n```json\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"user_id\": \"U0BGAB38H7C\",\n  \"bot_id\": null,\n  \"team\": \"hah\"\n}\n```\n\n**Identity warning (production helper text):**\n```\nSlack auth.test identified account \"default\" as user U0BGAB38H7C without bot_id. channels.slack.botToken appears to contain a user token; replace it with a Bot User OAuth Token. Until replaced, explicit bot-mention detection is disabled and required-mention channels fail closed.\n```\n\n**AFTER (fixed degraded publish):**\n```json\n{\n  \"connected\": true,\n  \"healthState\": \"degraded\",\n  \"lastError\": \"Slack auth.test identified account \\\"default\\\" as user U0BGAB38H7C without bot_id. channels.slack.botToken appears to contain a user token; replace it with a Bot User OAuth Token. Until replaced, explicit bot-mention detection is disabled and required-mention channels fail closed.\"\n}\n```\n\nNote: Full Socket Mode end-to-end status via Gateway also needs an App-Level Token (`xapp-…`); this L3 proves the identity gate + status publisher contract with live `auth.test` against the real workspace.\n\n### Agent Transcript\n- Cursor session: Slack L3 live identity/status proof (tokens redacted; rotate if exposed).\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
        "branch": "fix/slack-degraded-identity-status",
        "head_sha": "05cab1ac6368d2eba8916c9af5ab8994042fa308",
        "author": "zw-xysk",
